---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro'
import Chip from '../../components/Chip.astro'
import DocSection from '../../components/DocSection.astro'
import CommentsThreadDemo, { CommentsThreadTeamsDemo, options, teamOptions } from '../../demos/comments-thread'
import { api } from '../../api'
import { page } from '../../nav'
import { highlight } from '../../lib/highlight'

const codeHtml = await highlight(options)
const teamsHtml = await highlight(teamOptions)
---

<Docs current="comments-thread">
  <DocSection item={page('comments-thread')} api={api['comments-thread']}>
    <CommentsThreadDemo client:load codeHtml={codeHtml} />

    <section aria-labelledby="sending-title" class="flex flex-col gap-3 pt-8">
      <h2 id="sending-title" class="text-lg font-medium text-text-default">Sending and Retry</h2>
      <p class="text-base leading-6 text-text-muted">
        Return a promise from <Chip>onReply</Chip> and the comment shows at once, dimmed with a spinner, until it arrives in
        <Chip>comments</Chip> (same author, parent and text); then it takes the row's place without fading in again. A rejection
        leaves it with "Not sent", Retry, which gets focus, and Discard. In the demo, turn on Fail next send, then send a comment:
        it fails once, and Retry goes through.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="teams-title" class="flex flex-col gap-3 pt-8">
      <h2 id="teams-title" class="text-lg font-medium text-text-default">Other teams</h2>
      <p class="text-base leading-6 text-text-muted">
        Any record can carry a thread: a sales director agrees a discount on a deal and @mentions the account executive, a
        designer and a copywriter go over a campaign draft, and customer care leaves the warehouse an internal note on an order.
        That note is for the team only; a conversation with the customer is a support inbox, not this component.
      </p>
      <CommentsThreadTeamsDemo client:visible codeHtml={teamsHtml} />
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="delete-title" class="flex flex-col gap-3 pt-8">
      <h2 id="delete-title" class="text-lg font-medium text-text-default">Deleting with Undo</h2>
      <p class="text-base leading-6 text-text-muted">
        Delete never asks. The comment goes at once (a root with its replies), focus moves to the next comment or the composer,
        and a toast offers Undo with a countdown. <Chip>onDelete</Chip> runs only when that toast closes without Undo, or at once
        if the thread unmounts or the page is left first, so your API never deletes what was undone. Undo puts the comment back
        with focus on it; a rejected <Chip>onDelete</Chip> brings it back with an error toast. The toasts need the app's
        <Chip>&lt;Toaster /&gt;</Chip>. Delete shows on your own comments, and on everyone's with <Chip>moderator</Chip>, in the ⋯ menu. Edit
        sits next to Reply on your own comments, which say "(me)" after your name.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="mentions-title" class="flex flex-col gap-3 pt-8">
      <h2 id="mentions-title" class="text-lg font-medium text-text-default">Mentions</h2>
      <p class="text-base leading-6 text-text-muted">
        With <Chip>mentions</Chip>, "@" in the composer opens the Prompt bar's menu of the people <Chip>search</Chip> finds; it
        can return a promise. The composer is a Satin Textarea that takes that menu through its <Chip>underlay</Chip>, so a
        mention is a token in the text, removed whole with Backspace. <Chip>onReply</Chip> and <Chip>onEdit</Chip> get the
        mentions with their place in the body, and a comment's <Chip>mentions</Chip> are drawn as Free's Mention where the body
        reads "@" and the name.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="resolve-title" class="flex flex-col gap-3 pt-8">
      <h2 id="resolve-title" class="text-lg font-medium text-text-default">Resolve</h2>
      <p class="text-base leading-6 text-text-muted">
        <Chip>resolvable</Chip> puts Resolve at the start of the composer's row, away from Send. A resolved thread folds to one
        line, "Resolved by Marta Nowak", with Show comments and Reopen; it fades, it doesn't change height. Leave it uncontrolled
        (<Chip>defaultResolved</Chip>, and the resolver is <Chip>currentUser</Chip>) or control it with <Chip>resolved</Chip>,
        <Chip>onResolve</Chip> and <Chip>resolvedBy</Chip>. In the demo, resolve the thread once the offer is accepted.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="parts-title" class="flex flex-col gap-3 pt-8">
      <h2 id="parts-title" class="text-lg font-medium text-text-default">Parts</h2>
      <p class="text-base leading-6 text-text-muted">
        For a thread of your own, the pieces are exported: <Chip>Comment</Chip> (one article, with <Chip>state="sending"</Chip>
        or <Chip>"failed"</Chip>, <Chip>actions</Chip> and <Chip>footer</Chip>), <Chip>CommentComposer</Chip> (the field and
        Send, with mentions) and <Chip>CommentActions</Chip> (the ⋯ menu; the thread puts only Delete in it).
      </p>
    </section>
  </DocSection>
</Docs>
